Install the JAR locally and use as Maven dependency

Install your JAR in your local Maven repository:

mvn install:install-file ^
-Dfile="C:\Users\Chunnu\JavaLearning\NEXUS-X\nexus-security-common\target\nexus-security-common-1.jar" ^
-DgroupId=com.nexus.security.common ^
-DartifactId=nexus-security-common ^
-Dversion=1 ^
-Dpackaging=jar



Add it as a dependency in the consuming service's pom.xml:

<dependency>
    <groupId>com.nexus.security.common</groupId>
    <artifactId>nexus-security-common</artifactId>
    <version>1</version>
</dependency>


Use it in your code like any other dependency. All classes, beans, and configurations should now be available.